# Allow-list: exclude everything, then re-include only what the image needs.
# (Keeps raw datasets, SQLite files, vendor/, archive/, PDFs etc. out of the
# build context and out of the image.)
*

# The Dockerfile itself: remote builders (az containerapp up --source .,
# az acr build) filter their upload through THIS file, and without the
# Dockerfile they fall back to buildpack detection and build the wrong
# image. Local `docker build` reads it separately and never needed this.
!Dockerfile

!requirements.txt
!src/
!models/live_risk_lgbm.txt
!models/live_risk_meta.json
!data/processed/fitted_params.json
!data/processed/m5_weekly.npy

# Never ship these even though they live under src/
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
src/tests/
**/*.sqlite3*
